WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.005 --> 00:00:01.910
- I just had to ask this one question

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.680
'cause you've done so many,

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.600
so many films that everybody,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.050
I imagine anytime you get stopped,

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.130
it's always a different film

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.360
because there's so many

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.740
that are just, not just great,

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.030
maybe it just have such a great
impact on humanity overall.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.360
Like, whether it was,

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.003
you know, a deeper thing
or a lighter thing,

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:21.544
or any way or any sort,

00:00:21.544 --> 00:00:25.540
but I'm curious like, what
your favorite movie to do was.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.800
I know that's probably gotta be hard

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.900
'cause people ask me questions,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.930
but funny enough,

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.670
everybody always thinks
I love "The Bodyguard."

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.300
That is like, one of my
favorite movies of all time,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.510
but that's not my favorite of yours,

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.320
and this says something about me

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.860
that my favorite, I think
it's called "Mr. Brooks,"

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.740
and you're a serial killer.
- Yeah.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.470
- Okay, I love that one
because it was so out of pocket

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.550
and I thought that story was amazing,

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.383
how it did the twisting
- Yeah.

00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:47.216
- At the end,

00:00:47.216 --> 00:00:48.470
and I, it was just something

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:51.140
that was unpredictable
for me when I watched it,

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:51.973
but I was curious.

00:00:51.973 --> 00:00:52.806
What's one of yours?

00:00:52.806 --> 00:00:53.880
Like, what's one that sticks out

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.540
that like if it's on, you'll like, keep on

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.560
and not turn off?

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.710
- Well, I don't do that.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.283
I don't fall in love with
myself on the screen.

00:01:01.305 --> 00:01:02.138
You know--
- Not even

00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:02.971
if it's been like, years?

00:01:02.971 --> 00:01:04.590
Like, I mean like, years of watching--

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.190
- Sometimes, the kids would walk in

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.878
and they go, "Is that, that's you."

00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:10.920
- Yeah.
- And it's like,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.340
no, they won't let me turn it off

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.150
for a second and eventually,

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.143
I kinda have to walk out of the room.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.860
What I know in my heart

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.510
is that when you make a movie,

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.530
there's a chance for it to live forever,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.660
and it looks forever if it's fresh air,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.960
if it challenges you,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:31.980
if it makes you laugh,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.390
if it makes you cry,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.720
if it surprises you.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.170
Movies have all those things going for it,

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.930
but what they have is
they also have the ability

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.590
to do something that
you'll never ever forget.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.170
It's just hard, movies aren't easy.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.694
So, it's hard to make a great one.

00:01:47.694 --> 00:01:48.553
- I agree.

